<div class="exp-entry">
  <div class="exp-head"><h3>Berkeley AI Research (BAIR), EMBER Centre</h3><span class="exp-meta">Berkeley, CA · Apr 2026 – Present</span></div>
  <p class="exp-role">Machine Learning Research</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Advised by <a href="https://jonasfrey96.github.io/">Jonas Frey</a> and Siming He in Prof. Jitendra Malik's and Prof. Claire Tomlin's labs.</li>
    <li>First author of <a href="{{ '/assets/pdf/racing-the-clock.pdf' | relative_url }}">Racing the Clock: Teaching VLNs Budget-Conditioned Object Search</a>, <b>Best Paper Award</b> at the IROS 2026 Workshop on Intelligent Information Gathering. An extended version is under review at <b>ICRA 2027</b>.</li>
    <li>Compared an object-level Bellman expert that routes among targets using the full map with a room-level expert that reasons about unexplored rooms through doorway evidence and cross-scene priors, and distilled both into Uni-NaVid.</li>
    <li>Despite its lower expert return, room-level supervision gives the best student at every tested budget: at 2000 steps it finds <b>72.7%</b> of reachable targets, versus 68.5% for greedy-frontier supervision, 65.5% for object-level supervision, and 44.8% for the pretrained VLN.</li>
    <li>Awarded an <b>NSF grant</b> valued at <b>$150,000</b> in compute via ACCESS.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
